// Planted SAME KIND ACROSS CASES (27 Sep 2026, profile 1.6): a general claim that migration
// thins the forest, and a case in which herders' migration after drought thins theirs. The two
// migrations are one kind, not one state -- the text never joins them -- and so are the two
// forests; the census should find the case's step to be the general step again, and walk
// nothing between them.
===
title: "Kinds -- a general claim and its case"
mechanism:
    question: "Does migration thin the forest, and did it in the north?"
    levels: [macro, micro]
    actors:
        region:   {label: "The region", level: macro}
        herders:  {label: "Herding families in the north", level: micro}
        migrants: {label: "Rural migrants, in general", level: micro}
    kinds:
        migration: {label: "Rural-urban migration"}
        forest:    {label: "Forest cover"}
    states:
        drought:  {label: "Drought in the north", actor: region, role: condition}
        kmigr:    {label: "Herders' migration", actor: herders, kind: migration}
        kforest:  {label: "The north's forest cover", actor: region, kind: forest, role: outcome}
        migr:     {label: "Rural-urban migration", actor: migrants, kind: migration, role: condition}
        forest:   {label: "Forest cover", actor: region, kind: forest, role: outcome}
    chains:
        general: {label: "The general claim", question: "Does migration thin the forest?"}
        north:   {label: "The northern case", question: "What did drought do to the north's forest?"}
===

[Migration and forests]: Migration and forests are tied, in general and in the north.

[Migration thins forests]: Rural-urban migration thins the forest.
    {causes: {from: migr, to: forest, sign: "-", basis: asserted, chain: general}}
    +> [Migration and forests]

[Drought drove herders out]: Drought drove herding families to migrate.
    {causes: {from: drought, to: kmigr, sign: "+", basis: asserted, chain: north}}
    +> [Migration and forests]

[Their going thinned the north's forest]: Their going thinned the north's forest.
    {causes: {from: kmigr, to: kforest, sign: "-", basis: asserted, chain: north}}
    +> [Migration and forests]
